From a0a409c3091d3f9c7a2c0e4e0c3f4e2d9b1f0a2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: null cdev after thermal unregister

Adapted from upstream a0a409c3 ("wifi: mt76: mt7915: fix thermal zone
use-after-free"). The phy->tzone cleanup it adds refers to thermal-zone
support that does not exist at mt76 39c960c3, so it is dropped. Only the
phy->cdev reset is kept: without it, a second mt7915_unregister_thermal()
call unregisters a dangling cooling device.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7915/init.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/mt7915/init.c
+++ b/mt7915/init.c
@@ -186,6 +186,7 @@
 
 	sysfs_remove_link(&wiphy->dev.kobj, "cooling_device");
 	thermal_cooling_device_unregister(phy->cdev);
+	phy->cdev = NULL;
 }
 
 static int mt7915_thermal_init(struct mt7915_phy *phy)
